ck took next."}, {"turn": 14, "text": "The decisive blunder: H3 lost 16.4 points and moved Black's lead from +3.2 to +19.5. The engine wanted D4, on the left side where Black's D3 stone stood. Opus 5.5 played in the cramped bottom-right and never got back into the game."}, {"turn": 25, "text": "The 10k's only real slip was C1, which lost 7.2 points and cut Black's lead from +32.1 to +24.9. It hardly mattered, since Black was still far ahead and the engine's first choice there was C8."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "The only program run was libs.py, which parses a board the player pastes in and prints each group's stones and liberties; the other commands just read or appended to games.md notes. None of it chooses, ranks or looks ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}